        <body>
            <div xml:id="d706">

                <pb facs="0851" n="757" sameAs="frus:frus1896/pg757"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Williams to Mr. Uhl.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >United States Consulate-General</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Habana</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-03-28"><hi rendition="#italic">March 28, 1895</hi></date>.
                        (Received April 3.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 2462.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to previous correspondence
                    relating to Mr. Julio Sanguily, I beg to inclose for the imformation of the
                    Department a copy of the letter I addressed him on the 27th instant, informing
                    him of the decree of the Governor-General transferring his trial from the
                    military to the civil jurisdiction. I understand that he has appointed Don Pedro
                    Llorente, an eminent lawyer of Habana, for his defense. I was told that Don
                    Pedro would call to see me about the case, but I learn that he is sick, for
                    which reason I suppose he has not been able to come to the
                    consulate-general.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Ramon O. Williams</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Consul-General.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d706-a1.xml" xpointer="d706-a1"/>
            </div>
